                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Here we have a fairly basic VR mech fighting game. Aim with your motion controllers, move around a bit, use your super weapon when it charges up. Sometimes fight a boss - giant mech, squid mech, or a carrier with swarms of kamikaze fighters. You get crystals to upgrade your rig, and pick up various other weapons and power-ups. Combat feels super light, enemies are spongy. Graphics and audio are fine. Runs smooth enough, though sometimes when I pause to the menu my mech stops being able to move. I got this in a 10-game bundle for $4. Yes, I've gotten $0.40 of fun from it. Thumbs: UP! That being said, there are better VR mech sims out there if you want a really memorable experience.",
